@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Member C - ProposalReview work lifecycle\nMC-SM-0.1 internal candidate, 2026-09-12
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EEF4F8
skinparam stateBorderColor #27465B
skinparam ArrowColor #27465B
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D9

state QUEUED
state INVOKING
state VALIDATING
state RECOVERY_WAIT
state ACCEPTED
state HISTORICAL
state CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT

QUEUED : Complete accepted bundle; no trusted Risk result
INVOKING : Exactly selected invocation may return
VALIDATING : Candidate remains untrusted
RECOVERY_WAIT : Selected failed invocation retired
ACCEPTED : Immutable RiskReview stored; route its outcome
HISTORICAL : Retained result no longer current
CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT : No accepted RiskReview for this work

[*] --> QUEUED : admit [current authorised bundle]\n/ Domain.selectWork()
QUEUED --> INVOKING : start [G_START; current; budget]\n/ Domain.selectInvocation()
INVOKING --> VALIDATING : reply [G_EVENT]\n/ validate shape and bindings
INVOKING --> RECOVERY_WAIT : timeout [G_EVENT]\n/ Domain.retireSelectedInvocation()
VALIDATING --> RECOVERY_WAIT : invalidReply [G_EVENT]\n/ Domain.retireSelectedInvocation()
VALIDATING --> ACCEPTED : validReply [G_EVENT; current; valid outcome]\n/ Domain.storeReviewAndAuditAtomically()
RECOVERY_WAIT --> INVOKING : retry [G_EVENT; current; budget remains]\n/ Domain.selectNewRoundAndInvocation()
RECOVERY_WAIT --> CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT : exhausted [G_EVENT; no budget]\n/ Domain.recordActualFailureAndRoute()
QUEUED --> CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT : contextRetired [G_RETIRE]\n/ Domain.retireThisWork()
INVOKING --> CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT : contextRetired [G_RETIRE]\n/ Domain.retireThisWorkAndInvocation()
VALIDATING --> CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT : contextRetired [G_RETIRE]\n/ Domain.retireThisWorkAndInvocation()
RECOVERY_WAIT --> CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT : contextRetired [G_RETIRE]\n/ Domain.retireThisWork()
ACCEPTED --> HISTORICAL : proposal/input replaced or invalidated [G_RETIRE]\n/ Domain.removeCurrentAssociation(); preserve result
HISTORICAL --> [*]
CLOSED_WITHOUT_RESULT --> [*]

note right of ACCEPTED
  RiskReview.outcome is exactly one of:
  PASS -> Founder review
  PASS_WITH_WARNING -> visible warning
  REVISE -> new proposal and review
  NEEDS_INFORMATION -> Coordinator
  ESCALATE -> Founder, no direct approval
  These five outcomes are NOT lifecycle phases.
  No outcome creates approval or provider work.
end note
note left of INVOKING
  G_START: match selected work / round,
  with no invocation yet selected.
  G_EVENT: atomically match selected work,
  round and active invocation.
  In RECOVERY_WAIT, match the selected
  failed/retired invocation instead.
  Recheck current context and authority
  before new work or accepting a result.
end note
note left of HISTORICAL
  G_RETIRE: compare-and-set the exact
  selected work / association being retired;
  also match its invocation where present.
  Never retire a replacement round.
  Old PASS cannot authorise a new proposal.
end note
note right of RECOVERY_WAIT
  All obsolete reply, validation, timeout,
  retry and exhaustion events are no-ops
  for current state and business audit outcome.
  A new proposal creates new review work;
  it does not reset an old accepted result.
  Failure is not a sixth Risk outcome.
end note
legend bottom
Phases are conceptual internal modelling labels, not JSON fields or ReturnCase states.
Domain performs all authoritative actions; diagram arrows do not prove atomic runtime behaviour.
MC-D01/02/03 remain A/C decisions. Adapted from the shared report Figure 23 candidate.
endlegend
@enduml
